{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>These are the statutes.</b> All the commandments stated before the section beginning \"If in My statutes\" — these are the statutes, the judgments, and the teachings upon which the covenant was made with blessings and curses. This is the covenant he refers to when he says: מִלְּבַד הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַת אִתָּם בְּחֹרֵב (Deuteronomy 28:69)." "<b>Between Him and between the children of Israel.</b> That He, exalted be He, vowed the blessings when they merit, and they accepted the curses upon themselves if they do not merit. But the valuation of persons and the laws of consecrated house and field and firstborn and devoted items and animal tithe — all of these were stated after this covenant, even though they too were stated at Mount Sinai, as he says."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:25.753102340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}